---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { author } from '../data/author';
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { join } from 'node:path';

// Numbers that are static README-verbatim text (not in a sidecar), with their
// source in the demo at github.com/thrmnn/ros2-localization-triage:
//   TurtleBot3 to Tiago, "fired five times"         README.md, docs/transferability.md
//   recovery_alpha 0.0, the two ros2 param lines    docs/finding-amcl-recovery.md
// Everything else renders from public/data/*.json, written by
// scripts/sample-stata-replay.py from the demo's results/stata/.
const REPO = 'https://github.com/thrmnn/ros2-localization-triage';
const mailto = `mailto:${author.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('One incident')}`;

const readJson = (f: string) => JSON.parse(readFileSync(join(process.cwd(), 'public/data', f), 'utf8'));
const meta = readJson('stata-replay.meta.json') as {
  lost_window: { position_error_median_m: number; amcl_reported_sigma_median_m: number };
};
const base = readJson('stata-baseline.json') as {
  sigma_hindsight: { lost: number; healthy: number };
  detectors: { lost: number; healthy: number };
  detectors_events_starting_in_lost_window: number;
  lost_by_neither_hindsight: number;
};
if (base.sigma_hindsight.healthy !== base.detectors.healthy) {
  throw new Error('stata-baseline.json: the comparison is only fair at an equal healthy flag rate');
}
const lostMetres = meta.lost_window.position_error_median_m.toFixed(1);
const lostCm = Math.round(meta.lost_window.amcl_reported_sigma_median_m * 100);
---

<BaseLayout ogType="profile">
  <main class="page">
    <p class="who">
      <strong>Théo Hermann</strong>, independent practitioner. MSc Robotics, EPFL. Perception and autonomy work at EPFL VITA Lab, IRI Barcelona and Roboat, 2022 to 2024.
    </p>

    <h1>A localiser {lostMetres} metres wrong reported {lostCm} centimetres of uncertainty.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Your ROS 2 robots already record what happened. I read those recordings and tell you, in writing, what they show about an incident and what they cannot. Nothing goes on the robot.
    </p>
    <p class="ask">
      <a class="btn" href={mailto}>Send me one incident</a>
      <a href={author.cal} rel="noopener">or book 20 minutes</a>
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>If your monitoring trusts the robot's own uncertainty</h2>
      <p>On the recording behind that sentence: the check most teams write first, against mine, at the same rate of flags on healthy poses ({base.detectors.healthy}%).</p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Check</th><th scope="col">Lost poses flagged</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Threshold on the localiser's own uncertainty, picked knowing the answer</td><td class="n">{base.sigma_hindsight.lost}%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Four detectors (covariance spikes, transform jumps, disagreement with the wheels, gaps in the sensor stream), frozen before the run</td><td class="n">{base.detectors.lost}%</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="note">
        One public recording, one robot: a PR2 in MIT's Stata Center, replayed and graded by me against the dataset's ceiling AprilTags. The {base.detectors.lost}% is an upper bound ({base.detectors_events_starting_in_lost_window}% counting only detections that start in the lost window), and {base.lost_by_neither_hindsight}% of lost poses were flagged by neither. <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/finding-confidently-wrong.md`}>Source</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>If your alarms were tuned on one robot</h2>
      <p>Set on a simulated TurtleBot3, a covariance threshold sat inside the healthy noise of a real Tiago and fired five times on a recording with nothing wrong. A threshold belongs to the machine it was measured on, so I set yours on your recordings and measure how often each fires when nothing is wrong. <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/transferability.md`}>Source</a></p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>If you run Nav2, check this in one minute</h2>
      <p>Stock Nav2 ships AMCL with both recovery terms at 0.0, which leaves kidnap recovery switched off unless you change them. If both print 0.0, a displaced robot has no mechanism to conclude it is lost.</p>
      <pre><code>ros2 param get /amcl recovery_alpha_slow
ros2 param get /amcl recovery_alpha_fast</code></pre>
      <p class="note"><a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/finding-amcl-recovery.md`}>Source</a></p>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <h2>What you get</h2>
      <p><strong>One incident.</strong> Send the bag. You get back a written account: what happened, what the evidence supports, and what it does not.</p>
      <p><strong>Your fleet.</strong> Thresholds set on your own recordings, their measured rate on runs where nothing was wrong, and the scripts.</p>
      <p>Analysis runs on your infrastructure or under NDA on mine; nothing is retained after handover.</p>
      <p class="ask">
        <a class="btn" href={mailto}>Send me one incident</a>
        <a href={author.cal} rel="noopener">or book 20 minutes</a>
      </p>
      <p class="mail"><a href={mailto}>{author.email}</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="foot">
    <p>
      Every number on this page recomputes from <a href={REPO}>github.com/thrmnn/ros2-localization-triage</a>. Recorded data: MIT Stata Center dataset (CC BY 3.0), Universidad de León clean-and-attack recordings (CC BY 4.0).
    </p>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page, .foot { max-width: 38rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 20px; }
  .page { padding-top: 40px; color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .who { font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .who strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(30px, 6.4vw, 44px); line-height: 1.12; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 24px 0 16px; }
  .lede { margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .ask { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 12px 20px; margin: 0; }
  .btn {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 48px; padding: 0 22px;
    background: var(--text-primary); color: var(--bg-primary); border: 2px solid var(--text-primary);
    border-radius: 0; font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none;
  }
  .btn:hover { background: var(--bg-primary); color: var(--text-primary); }
  section { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 48px; padding-top: 32px; }
  h2 { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  section p + p, section p + table, section table + p, section pre + p { margin-top: 12px; }
  a { color: inherit; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .btn, .btn:hover { text-decoration: none; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 16px; }
  th { text-align: left; font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--text-primary); }
  th:last-child, td.n { text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; padding-left: 16px; }
  td { padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); vertical-align: top; }
  td.n { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .note { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; }
  pre { margin-top: 12px; padding: 12px 14px; border: 1px solid var(--border); overflow-x: auto; font: 14px/1.5 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; }
  #contact .ask { margin-top: 24px; }
  .mail { font-size: 16px; margin-top: 12px; }
  .foot { padding-top: 48px; padding-bottom: 40px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-secondary); }
</style>
